{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Update the gate_context.py 'RE-EXPORT CONTRACT' docstring (lines 36-47) to reflect that config no longer re-exports these names and that gate_context is now the canonical import path.","criteria":["maintainability"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["gate_context.py:36-43 'RE-EXPORT CONTRACT: every name below is re-exported from ``rebar.llm.config`` and NO consumer under ``src/`` imports it from here except ``gate_source.py``... Repointing a consumer here would leave those patches applying to a module the consumer no longer reads — the tests would pass while asserting nothing. Import from ``rebar.llm.config``, not from this module.'","config.py diff removes the entire `from rebar.llm.gate_context import (_active_code_root, ... assert_gated, current_code_sha, gate_session, ...)` re-export block","attest.py/manifest.py/remediation_mode.py/sidecar.py now do `from rebar.llm.gate_context import current_code_sha`; gate_source.py now does `from rebar.llm.gate_context import (gate_session, use_code_root, ...)`","tests/unit/test_llm_internal_shim_removal_2164_heldout.py:19-32 asserts rebar.llm.config no longer exports current_code_root/resolve_code_root/current_tickets_root/current_code_sha/in_gate_session/gate_session/assert_gated/use_code_root/use_tickets_root/_active_code_root/_active_tickets_root/_in_gate_session"],"finding":"The gate_context.py module docstring's 'RE-EXPORT CONTRACT' section is now stale and actively misleading: it asserts every gate-context name is re-exported from rebar.llm.config and commands 'Import from rebar.llm.config, not from this module', but this change deletes that re-export block from config.py, repoints all src consumers (attest.py, manifest.py, remediation_mode.py, sidecar.py, context_assembly.py, gate_source.py) to import directly from gate_context, and adds a heldout test asserting config must NOT export these names.","id":"0","impact":0.36,"location":"src/rebar/llm/gate_context.py:36","norm_id":"na3e744cad8b4706d","priority":0.36,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["A future maintainer adding a new gate-context consumer reads the docstring and imports from rebar.llm.config, hitting an ImportError (name no longer exported) or reintroducing the shim the ticket deleted."],"suggested_fix":"Rewrite the docstring's RE-EXPORT CONTRACT / dependency-direction paragraph to state that consumers now import gate-context names directly from rebar.llm.gate_context (and monkeypatch rebar.llm.gate_context.<name>), matching this migration and the heldout test.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"module","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":true,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"high","escapes_automation":true,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":false,"implicit_coupling":false,"likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":false,"removed_public_symbol":false,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":false,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_d